From: nexumia-de <https://github.com/nexumia-de>
Subject: wolfssljni: ignore freed sessions when updating session timeouts

SSLSessionContext.setSessionTimeout() walks every cached session and
sets its native timeout. A session whose WOLFSSL was freed when its
connection closed throws IllegalStateException("Object has been
freed"), which escapes to the caller. F-Droid sets the timeout in its
hostname verifier and crashes as soon as an earlier connection was
closed (e.g. after a mirror fallback).

Upstream wolfssljni catches this in setNativeTimeout() ("WOLFSSL freed
on connection close"); this is the minimal backport for the vendored
copy.

Upstream: https://github.com/wolfSSL/wolfssljni/blob/master/src/java/com/wolfssl/provider/jsse/WolfSSLImplementSSLSession.java
---
diff --git a/external/wolfssljni/src/java/com/wolfssl/provider/jsse/WolfSSLImplementSSLSession.java b/external/wolfssljni/src/java/com/wolfssl/provider/jsse/WolfSSLImplementSSLSession.java
index e5eb1a90..08cd9b40 100644
--- a/external/wolfssljni/src/java/com/wolfssl/provider/jsse/WolfSSLImplementSSLSession.java
+++ b/external/wolfssljni/src/java/com/wolfssl/provider/jsse/WolfSSLImplementSSLSession.java
@@ -550,7 +550,11 @@ public class WolfSSLImplementSSLSession implements SSLSession {
      * @param in timeout in seconds
      */
     protected void setNativeTimeout(long in) {
-        ssl.setSessTimeout(in);
+        try {
+            ssl.setSessTimeout(in);
+        } catch (IllegalStateException e) {
+            /* WOLFSSL freed on connection close */
+        }
     }
 
 
